    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Four-bedroom bungalow in spectacular elevated setting overlooking Lough Conn and across to the majestic Nephin Mountain.\r\n\r\nSet on an elevated site commanding truly breathtaking views across Lough Conn towards the majestic Nephin Mountain, this charming four-bedroom bungalow occupies one of the area’s most picturesque and tranquil settings.\r\n\r\nSurrounded by unspoilt beauty, this property enjoys a rural setting yet is within easy reach of Knockmore village (1.4km) and Foxford Town (8.4km) giving access to all amenities.\r\n\r\nAs the property has been vacant for just over two years, it may also be eligible for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, adding further value and appeal.\r\n\r\nThe property comprises two entrance halls, four bedrooms, a kitchen, living/dining area, separate sitting room and shower room. Oil-fired central heating provides warmth throughout, while generous off-street parking is available to the front, side and rear. To the rear, the garden provides an ideal space from which to relax and enjoy the exceptional surroundings and ever-changing views.\r\n\r\nKnockmore village closeby provides a grocery shop, church, national school, pub and GAA club, together with access to the wonderful recreational opportunities of Lough Conn, including stand-up paddleboarding and boating. The surrounding countryside is rich in natural beauty and heritage, with an abundance of scenic walking trails and renowned fishing locations close at hand.\r\n\r\nFoxford offers an excellent range of everyday amenities including shops, bars, restaurants and the renowned Foxford Woollen Mills. The town is beautifully positioned within easy reach of the Pontoon beaches, the River Moy and the Ox Mountains, providing an outstanding choice of outdoor pursuits and places to explore. Foxford is also well serviced by public transport, with a railway station and several bus routes providing convenient connections.\r\n\r\nWith Ballina, Swinford, Castlebar and Crossmolina all within commuting distance, this is a property that combines the tranquillity and beauty of rural living with excellent accessibility to surrounding towns and amenities. \r\n\r\nThis is an exciting opportunity to own a wonderful home in a truly spectacular setting."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway 3.17m (10'5\") x 2.49m (8'2\")\r\nBright entrance with a tiled floor and central pendant light.\r\n\r\nRear Entrance Hallway 1.45m (4'9\") x 2.03m (6'8\")\r\nBright entrance with lino flooring, central pendant light, and glass panelled door providing ample natural light.\r\n\r\nSitting Room 2.9m (9'6\") x 4.33m (14'2\")\r\nWith timber flooring, central pendant light, solid fuel stove, and a large window overlooking Lough Conn and Nephin Mountain.\r\n\r\nKitchen 2.08m (6'10\") x 3.67m (12'0\")\r\nFitted kitchen with a tiled floor, tiled splashback, tongue and groove ceiling, integrated oven, hob, microwave and under-counter space for a washing machine. A large window provides ample natural light.\r\n\r\nLiving/Dining Area 3.56m (11'8\") x 4.51m (14'10\")\r\nSpacious room with a tiled floor, tongue and groove ceiling, stanley range with brick surround, and a large window overlooking Lough Conn and Nephin Mountain.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 3.3m (10'10\") x 2.1m (6'11\")\r\nSingle room with timber flooring, central pendant light and a large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 3.04m (10'0\") x 3.33m (10'11\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, central pendant light and a large window providing natural light and beautiful views across Lough Conn to Nephin Mountain.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 2.37m (7'9\") x 3.3m (10'10\")\r\nSingle room with timber flooring, central pendant light and a large window providing natural light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 3.24m (10'8\") x 4.19m (13'9\")\r\nDouble room with timber flooring, central pendant light and a large window providing natural light and beautiful views across Lough Conn to Nephin Mountain. This room also features an ensuite.\r\n\r\nWet Room 2.38m (7'10\") x 2.51m (8'3\")\r\nFully tiled wet room with shower, toilet, and floating sink."
      },
